# Tangle's attacking creatures are the ones attacking as it resolves (its ruling; CR 611.2c: the effect changes no
# rule of the game, so its set is fixed then). Cast in Bot1's first main phase, it finds none: Raging Goblin attacks
# afterwards, its combat damage is still prevented this turn (CR 615.1), and it untaps in Bot1's next untap step.

[Bot1 Deck]
Mountain
Raging Goblin
Island x18

[Bot2 Deck]
Forest
Mox Emerald
Tangle
Island x17

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mountain.Play
Bot1.Battlefield.Mountain.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Raging Goblin.Cast
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Forest.Play
Bot2.Hand.Mox Emerald.Cast
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot2.Battlefield.Forest.Activate
Bot2.Battlefield.Mox Emerald.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Tangle.Cast
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Pass
? Stack.Count = 0
Bot1.Attack(Raging Goblin > Bot2)
[T3 Bot1.Main2]
? Bot2.Life = 20
? Bot1.Battlefield.Raging Goblin.Tapped = true
? Bot1.Battlefield.Raging Goblin.DoesntUntap = (absent)
[T5 Bot1.Upkeep]

[Expect]
Bot2.Life = 20
Bot1.Battlefield.Raging Goblin.Tapped = false
Bot2.Graveyard = Tangle
